course: dictionary
lesson: 3560
title: Ferment: change, trouble and excitement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «Yeast ferments the sugar in bread dough.» Here the sentence is about science, so ferment means to change chemically, because tiny living things break down sugar and make gas. Ask yourself what is happening in the sentence, then pick the meaning that fits.
explain: «The crowd was in a ferment, shouting and pushing at the gates.» The words shouting and pushing are your clue. People who are in a ferment are stirred up, restless and excited, not calm. This use is formal, so you will often see it in history books and news stories.
explain: A word can also be a noun. «The village was in a state of ferment after the flood.» Here ferment is a thing you can be in, like a mood. If you are not sure, swap in a word you know, such as «in a state of trouble», and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Ferment is a verb and a noun: you can ferment something, or be in a ferment.
fact: To ferment means to change because of yeast or bacteria, which break down sugar and make gas, acid or alcohol.
fact: Bread rises because yeast ferments the sugar in the dough.
fact: Yoghurt, cheese, sauerkraut, kimchi and soy sauce are all made by fermentation.
fact: «In a ferment» means excited, restless or in trouble. It is a formal phrase, so you will see it in older books and news.
exercise: «Farmers let the cocoa beans ferment under leaves for several days.» What does ferment mean here? | Stay still and fresh | Turn into sugar in a day | Freeze solid in the sun | *Slowly change and turn a little sour, helped by tiny living things
exercise: «Only after fermenting, drying and roasting do the cocoa beans start to smell of chocolate.» What must happen before the beans smell of chocolate? | Being mixed with fish | Being frozen in a shop | *Fermenting, drying and roasting | Nothing, they smell of chocolate at once
exercise: «The crowd was in a ferment, shouting and pushing at the gates.» What does in a ferment mean? | Quiet and happy | Calm and sleepy | Hungry and tired | *Restless, stirred up and excited
test: Yeast makes bread rise. What does yeast do to sugar? | *Breaks it down and makes gas | Keeps it fresh and unchanged | Freezes it | Turns it into ice
test: To ferment trouble means to stir it up. Which word is closest in meaning? | Forget | Freeze | *Foment | Calm
exam: Which of these foods is made by fermentation? | Boiled sweets | *Yoghurt | Plain salad | Ice lollies
